s8-5-p4 = prose (cons "A representation changes a type by an equivalence or relates a concrete state to an abstract state by a stated relation. These are different objects. When an equivalence is available, univalence supplies transport. When information is hidden or discarded, the relation or quotient must say what is hidden. The graph equivalence (3.6)–(3.7) provides the information-preserving factorization; observational refinements are defined in §8.2." nil)
